From 4bf1579520315b048c1b348fa234a750e2f364f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:26:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] coreclr: /EHa semantics for the Itanium C++ EH of
 clang/MinGW

CoreCLR's Windows code relies on MSVC /EHa: destructors run when an SEH
exception (access violation, managed exception) unwinds a frame, and
catch(...) (EX_CATCH) catches SEH exceptions. libunwind/libc++abi ignore
foreign exceptions. minipal/Windows/mingw_eha.cpp adds that behaviour,
linked into coreclr.dll and clrjit.dll with lld --wrap:
- __gxx_personality_seh0: for SEH exceptions, phase 1 takes the
  exception into a catch(...) found in the LSDA (wrapped into a C++
  exception object); phase 2 enters cleanup landing pads by collided
  unwinds and resumes the unwind after them;
- _Unwind_Resume: resumes those unwinds;
- __C_specific_handler: Windows' semantics, plus the bookkeeping that
  lets C++ cleanups run during the unwinds an __except starts (also for
  C++ exceptions caught by __except);
- __cxa_rethrow: "throw;" re-raises a caught SEH exception;
- CLR_MinGW_RtlUnwind for the managed exception dispatch (ClrUnwindEx).
Unwinds are described by a record whose EXCEPTION_RECORD copy is tagged,
so that the handlers of every module can resume them.
mingw_guids.cpp: IID_IInspectable, missing from mingw-w64's libuuid.
